<%# The scribe, and the only place in the app he appears: he needs room to read, and the
    32px header mark is not it. Cross-legged, tablet across the lap, reed pressed into the
    clay — the edubba's whole job in one shape.

    Two shapes had to go to get there. A shin under the tablet turns the whole thing into a
    monitor on a stand, so the legs are a crossed mound instead; and a stylus angled up out
    of the hand reads as an aerial, so the reed runs through the hand and down into the
    clay, which is how it is actually held. %>
<svg class="<%= local_assigns[:class_name] %>" viewBox="0 0 96 96" fill="none"
     stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
  <circle cx="38" cy="17" r="8" />
  <path d="M35.5 24.5c-4.5 4-7 9.5-7 16v4" />
  <path d="M24 66c0-7 6-12.5 13-12.5h8c7 0 13 5.5 13 12.5Z" />
  <path d="M18 66h46" />
  <path d="M28 41.5c10-2.4 20-2.4 30 0 1.2 4.2 1.2 8.4 0 12.6-10 2.4-20 2.4-30 0-1.2-4.2-1.2-8.4 0-12.6Z"
        fill="currentColor" fill-opacity=".1" />
  <path d="M34 47h13M34 51.5h9" stroke-width="2.2" />
  <path d="M36 26.5c5 4.5 8 8.5 8.5 13" />
  <%# The reed crosses the arm at the hand rather than running alongside it: parallel and
      adjacent, the two strokes merge into one thick diagonal at any size that matters. %>
  <path d="m52 29-8.5 15" stroke-width="2.2" />
</svg>
